				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## First image increment — 2026-10-20\nOwner CatalystDevKit / BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core, GT/Pharo only. Contract: {{gtPage:Catalyst Fairy|db=731asfxqhyhdr96k6wo9yxnzv}} and user-accepted design: developer right bubbles with Font Awesome user; Barry left documents with transparent fairy; bottom composer; inherited renderer/model/history. This is a first bounded increment, not completion of observability.\n\n{{gtMethod:BVCFairyChat>>#asElement}} now selects {{gtClass:BVCFairyChatElement}} under the unchanged Barry header/instructions action. Generic GtLChat remains unchanged. The subclass selects {{gtClass:BVCFairyDeveloperMessageElement}} and {{gtClass:BVCFairyReplyMessageElement}} only locally via initializeListElement/messageElementClassFor:. Developer bubble uses rounded geometry, translucent fill, FontAwesomeIcons #user, and asymmetric list margins (80 left / 5 right), not right-aligned text. Barry has transparent background, no shadow bubble, and the existing transparent fairy image in its header. Existing content expanders, tool integration, response model views and execution states remain inherited.\n\ninitialize and updateElement retain the existing GtLNewMessageElement and existing newMessageViewModel as a sibling after the scrolling list, excluding that draft from list items. Draft editor is not rebound on message updates. No new transcript/provider/model/client. The former generic list auto-scroll-to-last is deliberately omitted: no forced jumps, but follow-at-bottom behavior remains unimplemented. Existing 300ms BrElementUpdater and renderer subscriptions are reused; no new provider streaming capability is claimed."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
